WEBVTT

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.600
<i>Congratulations to Kaito for his magnificent victory!</i>

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.550
<i>Now he will be the second semifinalist after Tron!</i>

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.180
<i>Only two positions remain open!</i>

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:13.940
<i>Who will advance and take those spots?!</i>

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.440
<i>I'm sure the hearts of all Dueling fans around the world are pumped!</i>

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.530
<i>Now, everyone, together with me!</i>

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.670
<i>Heart Burning!</i>

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:32.670
If Tron and Dr. Faker are gonna use their own children as tools for revenge,

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.510
I won't forgive them!

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.030
Yuma, there is a strong resonance from the left side.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.190
Resonance?

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.890
Is this the power of crests III and V had?

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:50.450
That must mean Tron's up ahead!

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.370
The probability is... high.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:54.630
Okay! Let's go!

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:05.120
<i>Now, this is the Magma Field!</i>

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:09.960
<i>Just who will come to this scorching hot field?!</i>

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:19.680
It's Shark! He's so cool!

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.260
Geez, it won’t be fun without Yuma!

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:29.090
I finally caught you. You won't escape any longer!

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.700
Heh, you've got a terrible personality.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:34.940
It's not like I was running away.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.690
I was merely pretending so I could lure you here.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:40.030
Right into this scorching hot Magma Field.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:46.970
Because in this world of boiling hot fire,
 you have the utmost disadvantage.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.900
And that's because your deck is Water-Attribute based.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:53.060
Your Monsters won't be able to survive long here.

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:59.340
Ah, IV-<i>sama</i>! I'm looking forward to your service today!

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.930
Service my butt. These guys don't know this guy's true personality.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.070
IV's true personality... You mean...

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.440
He's a devil!

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:11.000
Duel!!

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:15.090
The first turn belongs to me!
 My turn! Draw!

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:17.240
The Scorching Hot Magma Field, huh?

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.200
Don't take me lightly!

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.450
I activate the Quick-Play Magic, Plate Salvage!

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:28.760
Due to its effect, the Field Magic is negated for two turns!

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.840
Shark... And IV!

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:43.550
Yuma.

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:45.260
So he came.

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:48.540
But this is the Magma Field, isn't it?

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:50.580
It's not hot at all.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.130
As expected of Shark.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.630
It seems he stopped the Field Magic by using a Magic Card.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.770
It's finally begun.

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:05.660
This is an important battle between IV and Ryouga.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:08.480
Now, fight to your heart's content.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:11.660
So I can confirm it with my own eyes.

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:21.820
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:27.160
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:44.010
<i>Hey, my friends, what scenery do you suppose</i>

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:49.810
<i>awaits us on the other side of this hill?</i>

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:54.400
<i>Hey, my friends, let's climb it together</i>

00:03:55.770 --> 00:04:00.440
<i>It's too late for us to turn back now</i>

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:05.530
<i>The time has come to combine
 together the power dwelling inside me</i>

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:11.080
<i>Gotta release my Soul Drive</i>

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:16.880
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:21.920
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:27.390
<i>Keep running, keep running, until you get there</i>

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:33.060
<i>Once again, once again, keep those challenges coming</i>

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:39.230
<i>My friends, keep on living in the here and now</i>

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:45.320
<i>Keep pressing onward together no matter what happens</i>

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:49.010
I Summon Tripod Fish!

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.820
Then, when there is a Fish-Type Monster on my field,

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.700
I can Special Summon this guy from my hand!

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:07.490
Come! Shark Sucker!

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:16.290
"Number 57: Shark Torpedoed! 
The Nightmarish Fanservice"

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.790
He's got two Level Three Monsters!

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:15.500
Which means from the get go…?!

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.000
An Xyz Summon!

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:21.920
I Overlay the Level Three Tripod Fish and Shark Sucker!

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:27.340
Xyz Summon!

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:31.260
Come forth, Submersible Carrier Aero Shark!

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.850
I activate Aero Shark’s Monster Effect!

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:37.350
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:41.520
it inflicts 400 damage to my opponent for each card in my hand!

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:43.940
I have three cards in my hand.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.450
So that's 1200 points of damage!

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:55.200
Clever!

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.080
He gave his opponent Effect Damage on his first turn!

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.290
Shark is so awesome!

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:04.920
Yeah! Nice one, Shark!

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:08.260
To summarize, we're on your side here!

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:11.760
I set two cards face-down and end my turn!

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:19.600
Quite interesting that you were able to Summon an Xyz Monster in the very beginning.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:21.190
It makes crushing you all the more rewarding!

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:23.520
My turn! Draw!

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:27.900
When there is no Monster on my field while you control an Xyz Monster,

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:32.330
I can Special Summon Gimmick Puppet Magne Doll from my hand!

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:35.540
Mag...net!

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.250
Then I Summon Gimmick Puppet Gear Changer!

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:46.050
This card can become the same level of a Gimmick Puppet on the field!

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:47.840
Gear Up!

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:49.630
Gear Changer!

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:57.480
Now IV has two Monsters with the same level as well.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:58.180
Here it comes!

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:04.020
I Overlay the Level Eight Gimmick Puppet Magnet Doll and Gimmick Puppet Gear Changer!

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:09.860
I use these two Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:11.860
Xyz Summon!

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:16.080
Come forth, Number 15!

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.080
Gimmick Puppet Giant Killer!

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.290
That's...!

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:23.500
He played it!

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:26.420
The Number that tormented Tetsuo and the Class Rep.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:33.470
If you're going to come at me seriously, I'll return the gesture.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:36.600
I'll show you the greatest fanservice there is!

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.020
What's that Monster?

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:42.980
IV-<i>sama</i>?

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:48.360
<i>Whoops, what in the world?! What on earth is happening?!</i>

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.950
<i>During this fan-favorite, highly-anticipated showdown between Shark and IV,</i>

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.660
<i>What an accident to occur!</i>

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.740
<i>The anger in my heart is about to make it explode!</i>

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:58.330
<i>Heart Burning!</i>

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:02.040
<i>Is this their doing?</i>

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:05.540
Sorry about that!

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:08.380
Since the following contents will be too inappropriate for people to watch,

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:11.010
I took the liberty of destroying all your cameras.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:16.220
So, IV, send Ryoga to the abyss of darkness.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.060
Force him to his knees!

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:23.560
I activate Gimmick Puppet Giant Killer’s Monster Effect!

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:29.860
It destroys Xyz Monsters on the field, and inflicts damage to my opponent equal to their total Attack Powers!

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:35.950
Oh crap!

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:51.340
Shark!

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:57.050
Then I attack directly with Gimmick Puppet Giant Killer!

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:01.390
I activate the Permanent Trap, Bubble Bringer!

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:05.520
This card can negate my opponent’s direct attack!

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:08.060
Phew…He just blocked that.

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:10.070
Oh well.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:13.990
When my turn ends, Plate Salvage’s effect will vanish too.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.320
You'll feel the scorching Hell next time!

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:19.450
I end my turn!

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.960
What the? Oh, hot!

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.460
It really is like a scorching Hell.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.970
So this is the Field Magic, Magma Ocean!

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.810
Decide whether I'm showing off or not only after you watch my Duel!

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.390
My turn! Draw!

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:48.020
I Summon Hammer Shark!

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:53.110
Then I activate Bubble Bringer’s effect!

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:55.610
By sending this card to the Graveyard,

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:59.030
in exchange, I Special Summon Tripod Fish from my Graveyard!

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:05.080
When it's Special Summoned successfully, Tripod Fish’s level is increased by one!

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:08.750
You fool!

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:14.840
Thanks to the Field Magic, Magma Ocean, when a Water-Attribute Monster is Summoned, it is destroyed!

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:18.470
You Monsters will never be able to survive here!

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:20.140
Eat this!

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:30.480
What?!

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:32.400
What happened?

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:33.520
It's a Trap Card.

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:35.480
It activated on Shark's field.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:38.070
What's that?!

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:41.160
The Permanent Trap Card, Adapting to Adversity!

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:45.660
This card can negate the effects of Magic or Traps that destroys a Monster!

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:50.620
Now my Monsters can survive in this scorching Hell as well!

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:53.500
Amazing! That's Shark for you!

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:57.260
The spirit he's betting this match on is extraordinary.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:04.260
<i>IV… I was framed by you in the National Championships.</i>

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:09.190
<i>Then my younger sister, who had nothing to do with this, was also hurt by you!</i>

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:10.730
<i>I will never...</i>

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:12.690
<i>...forgive you!</i>

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:18.110
I will defeat you using any means necessary!

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:20.910
Yuma, he's serious about this.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:22.570
Don’t tell me Shark…

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:26.870
The Monster special summoned by Bubble Bringer’s effect

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:28.580
can be treated as two Xyz Materials!

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:34.170
I Overlay Tripod Fish, which is now treated as two, Xyz Materials and Hammer Shark!

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:38.460
I use these three Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:39.920
Xyz Summon!

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:44.720
Come forth, Number 32!

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:52.520
Marine Biting Dragon - Shark Drake!

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:58.940
That's from before!

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:00.150
The Number!

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:04.620
Yes, the Number III gave Ryoga.

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:07.370
By my orders, mind you.

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:11.540
I've been waiting for this moment, Ryoga.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:16.130
In order to spread the darkness in your heart even more!

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:18.960
That's III's...

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:23.180
I knew V and Tron were plotting something, but...

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:26.350
They actually utilized III to give this Number to Ryoga?!

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:29.220
Although I never told you that.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:31.640
Tron...! Why?!

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:35.980
Well, if I told you, there was a chance you could leak our plan!

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.110
You've got a loose tongue, after all.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.610
Everyone has their own role.

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:47.070
V has V's. III has III's.

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:49.990
And mine... What's <i>my</i> role?!

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:55.580
To beat Ryoga into the abyss of darkness!

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.420
Everything has been going well so far.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.800
Just as I planned.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.260
Cornering him to this degree,

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:06.090
And forcing him to Summon Shark Drake...
 Are those in your plan too?!

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:07.970
That's right.

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:12.810
You could be in danger if you get careless.

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:19.900
You know the power of Ryoga and his Shark Drake well, don't you?

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:21.940
Ryoga's power?

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:25.280
Go! Shark Drake!

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.320
Attack Gimmick Puppet Giant Killer!

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:36.620
I then activate Shark Drake’s effect!

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:38.880
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:44.550
it lowers the Attack Power of the Gimmick Puppet Giant Killer I just destroyed by 1000,

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:47.130
and Special Summons it to IV’s field!

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:50.140
Why would he return the opponent’s Monster?

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:52.060
Well, uh...

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:58.520
Shark Drake can attack the Monster Special Summoned by this effect once again.

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:00.310
And there you have it, Kotori.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:01.360
Huh? What?

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:03.900
IV's only got 1500 Life left.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:06.200
If this goes through, Shark wins!

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.330
I won't let you!

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.660
I Special Summon Gimmick Puppet Night Joker from my hand!

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:29.340
This card can be Special Summoned by banishing the Giant Killer in my Graveyard!

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:34.600
That sure was a <i>close one</i>!

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:37.810
But I admit your response in that moment was very impressive.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:40.270
Now you can continue to fight.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:44.230
Which means you can corner Ryoga even further!

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:50.160
You spared your life, IV. I'll end my turn there!

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:53.410
Look there! Ryoga's still into this!

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:54.660
You have to try harder!

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.620
I <i>know</i> that!!

00:14:58.460 --> 00:14:58.960
Eh?

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:00.540
Who's IV... talking to?

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:03.340
I <i>know</i> that!

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:08.260
My mission is to beat Ryoga into the darkness of his heart!

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:09.680
For that, everything up until now...

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.640
Calumniating him in the tournament...

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.810
Heavily injured his younger sister...

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:18.680
Everything was for the sake of you, Tron!
 I followed your orders this entire time!

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.150
Huh? Tron's orders?!

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:23.150
What's he mean?!

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:27.860
Are you here, Tron?! Hurry up and show yourself!

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:28.990
I'm right here.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.320
You bastard!

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:32.820
Tron's over there?!

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:36.160
He's probably using some kind of power

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:39.080
to allow only one person to sense his presence.

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:42.250
Bingo! I'd expect no less from you, Astral.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:45.710
Tron! What is your aim?

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.050
Cornering Shark...

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:49.840
Beating the darkness out of his heart...

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:51.260
What are you doing it all for?!

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:53.720
Since there is no need to hide anything,

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:55.800
I will just answer everyone.

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:05.480
The reason I decided to beat Ryouga’s heart into the darkness

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.020
is so I can manipulate him.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:09.690
And use him as an assassin to go after Dr. Faker.

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:11.400
Assassin?!

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:15.700
Stop joking! I'm not interested the least bit in doing that!

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:19.830
Even you don’t want to, you can’t escape anymore!

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:23.210
You will become my puppet to manipulate.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:25.130
My own personal doll.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:29.000
Me and my brothers fought with all we had for your sake, Tron!

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:31.050
So why are you not after us...

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:33.180
No, why are you after Ryoga and not us?!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.300
I can't accept that!

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:38.470
Like I told you, everyone has their own role.

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:44.350
When it comes to defeating Dr. Faker, Ryoga is far more...

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:49.270
I won't accept it! I will <i>never</i> accept that!

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:51.490
<i>I</i> will defeat Dr. Faker!

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:53.490
Not a guy like <i>him</i>!

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:56.030
I'll show you that I'm strong enough to do it!

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:58.080
My turn! Draw!

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:03.620
I activate the Magic Card from my hand, Puppet Ritual!

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:10.170
This card can call a “Gimmick Puppet” Monster from my Graveyard back to my field!

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.720
Come, Gimmick Puppet Magne Doll!

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:25.140
I Overlay the Level Eight Gimmick Puppet Night Joker and Gimmick Puppet Magne Doll!

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:31.110
I use these two Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.360
Xyz Summon!

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:36.570
Show yourself, Number 40!

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.410
Gimmick Puppet Heaven’s Strings!

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:51.300
Then I activate the Equip Magic from my hand, Destiny Strings!

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:54.210
And I equip it to Gimmick Puppet Heaven’s Strings!

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:02.060
By sending a card from my deck to the Graveyard,

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:04.310
if that card is a Monster Card,

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:07.810
the equipped Monster can attack up to the same number of that Monster’s level,

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:11.020
without destroying your Monster!

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:16.280
The one I drew is the Level Eight Gimmick Puppet Necro Doll!

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:24.080
Thus it can attack Shark Drake eight times!

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:26.750
What'd he say?!

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:28.710
He can attack eight times in a row?!

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:30.920
Do it, Heaven's Strings!

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:32.540
Heaven's Blade!!

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:44.220
Shark!

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:46.600
According to Destiny String’s effect,

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:51.060
without destroying the Monster, it can attack consecutively and inflict damage!

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.730
Continue, Heaven’s Strings!

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:56.400
Torment Shark Drake nice and good!

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:03.240
Suffer! Suffer even <i>more</i>, Ryoga!

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:11.040
He can't...

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:14.210
Stop it! This isn't a Duel!

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:17.590
Dueling does not exist for rage and revenge!

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:19.630
I will not let you interfere.

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:25.600
I can't move!

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:27.140
Yuma!

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:30.810
The entertainment is just getting started from here on out, after all.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:33.270
Be a good boy and watch from over there.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:38.400
No! Stop already!

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:41.110
Dueling is something that makes people happy!

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:43.240
Keep suffering, Ryoga...

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:47.120
Suffer, suffer more, and agonize before falling into Hell!

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:49.120
This is the fifth attack!

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:56.040
As long as they Duel, everyone can become fiends, or even companions!

00:19:56.960 --> 00:20:00.010
Hurting each other isn't Dueling at all!

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:02.430
Become friends with everyone, eh?

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:04.930
You really <i>are</i> just like him.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.390
Like Kazuma Tsukumo.

00:20:08.390 --> 00:20:09.180
Tron...!

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:14.060
He did say that pretty often too. Something like “friendship” and “making people happy”.

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:17.610
I-If you all didn't get my father involved into this in the first place…!

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:19.110
Yuma...

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:23.240
The one who took your father away from you is Dr. Faker.

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:25.320
If you have anyone to hate, it should be Faker.

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:30.540
Doing so, the darkness will be born inside your heart.

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:31.830
Then it will spread.

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:37.460
I did promise you, after all, that I will eat your heart out next time.

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:40.760
Stop joking! I won’t forgive you!

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:43.050
You're the one who made Droite suffer!

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:46.680
And you're the one who used III and V as tools for revenge!

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:50.810
Not bad. The darkness in your heart is growing.

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:55.100
The hatred will amplify that darkness. Feel free to hate.

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:56.650
And Dr. Faker!

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:58.320
Shut your mouth!

00:20:58.360 --> 00:20:59.650
Now here comes the last one!

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:06.490
How was it, Ryoga?
 But it isn't over yet!

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:10.450
I activate Gimmick Puppet Heaven’s Strings’ Monster Effect!

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:16.630
By detaching one Overlay Unit, it places a String Counter on Shark Drake!

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:39.190
When next turn ends, Shark Drake will be destroyed,

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:43.490
and you will take damage equal to its original Attack Power.

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:47.570
Then we'll have a true farewell!
 I'll end my turn with that!

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:49.990
Shark...

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:52.830
Shark! Answer me!

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:55.410
Hey, you can hear me, can't you, Shark?!

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:57.040
Shark!

00:21:57.960 --> 00:21:59.880
Shark... can't be...!

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:04.170
Shark!

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:15.560
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:22:15.810 --> 00:22:21.190
<i>Move on ahead, speeding up our throbbing beats</i>

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:31.870
<i>Listen boys and girls, here's the secret to boys and girls like you</i>

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:36.120
<i>You're really just so spontaneous, wild as can be</i>

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:37.410
<i>I bet you didn't know?</i>

00:22:37.660 --> 00:22:40.130
<i>You might be a handful, but what's wrong with that?</i>

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:42.750
<i>Be up to no good, but learn for real</i>

00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:47.970
<i>Go the unpredictable route and shuffle your cards with a goal in mind</i>

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:53.310
<i>Whenever you feel like you've lost your way, just take a minute to close your eyes...</i>

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:58.940
<i>Shout "stop!" with all you've got, and there's your boundary line.</i>

00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:05.400
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:10.910
<i>We won't just stop here, not when we don't want to have any regrets.</i>

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:16.160
<i>Even if we get hurt, we can't just hesitate now</i>

00:23:16.370 --> 00:23:21.750
<i>We won't just give up, not when our future's a lot brighter than our today</i>

00:23:21.750 --> 00:23:27.010
<i>Seriousness... It'll only make us keep fighting even harder</i>

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:32.510
<i>We'll always get as fascinated as we want, and we'll fight on every day</i>

00:23:41.100 --> 00:23:43.860
Although he was heavily injured, Shark stands and continues to fight!

00:23:44.310 --> 00:23:46.980
But IV’s onslaught is still ongoing mercilessly.

00:23:47.570 --> 00:23:49.490
Under these overwhelmingly disadvantaged circumstances,

00:23:49.490 --> 00:23:52.660
the only method left for victory is…

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:54.820
IV’s trump? Don’t tell me…!

00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:57.200
Why would you give power to him?

00:23:57.330 --> 00:23:59.790
Tron, you bastard!

00:24:00.370 --> 00:24:01.920
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal!

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:05.210
"Shark Awakens! A New Chaos Number Appears"

00:24:05.210 --> 00:24:08.960
No, Shark, stop it!

00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:13.680
Today we'll be introducing Number 32, Shark Drake!

00:24:13.800 --> 00:24:16.260
It can attack the Monster is just defeated.

00:24:16.390 --> 00:24:18.770
Quite shark-like to not let its prey escape.

00:24:20.430 --> 00:24:20.980
What's wrong, Yuma?

00:24:21.230 --> 00:24:24.480
We ran out of time before I could explain the gag!
